      "role": "user",
      "content": "im in the middle of a production outage and my gke cluster is acting up. i have a pod in CrashLoopBackOff and i can't tell if it's hitting a resource limit or if the liveness probe is just failing. \n\nhere is the describe output:\n```\nName:         api-service-7f8db9-x2z9l\nNamespace:    production\nStatus:       Running\nContainers:\n  api-service:\n    State:          Waiting\n      Reason:       CrashLoopBackOff\n    Last State:     Terminated\n      Reason:       Error\n      Exit Code:    1\n    Liveness:       http-get http://:8080/healthz delay=30s timeout=1s period=10s #success=1 #failure=3\nEvents:\n  Warning  Unhealthy  kubelet  Liveness probe failed: Get \"http://10.48.1.15:8080/healthz\": dial tcp 10.48.1.15:8080: connect: connection refused\n```\n\ncan u give me a quick checklist to figure out if i need to bump the memory limits or if the app is just not ready when the probe hits? i need to know exactly what commands to run to check the exit code and the actual network binding. no fluff pls, just the steps.",
